-- title:
--   Assembling the q=2 supersingular affine chart with residual transcendence
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $q$ is a prime subject to $q = 2$ (hypothesis `hq2`), $M'$ is a non-zero natural number with $q \nmid M'$, and a rigidifying prime $\ell_g$ is fixed with $\ell_g \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ and $\ell_g \mid M'$. Further, $A$ is a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} =$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ` lying over $q$ in the sense of [`ValuationSubring.LiesOverPrime`](def/FLTPrelim_Ramification.html#L16), i.e. $q$ is a non-unit of $A$; $\kappa =$ `ResidueField A` denotes its residue field. The finite set $W$ of places of `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'` over $\kappa$ (that field being generated over $\kappa$ by `jqModC κ` and its $M'$-fold $q$-expansion rescaling `jqNModC κ M'`) is required by `hW` to consist exactly of the members of `ssPlaces q M' κ`, namely the places $w$ that are rational (the structure map $\kappa \to$ residue field of $w$ is surjective), satisfy the predicate `IsAffineGeomPlace`, and whose value $w.\mathrm{evalAt}(\mathtt{jGeomGen κ M'})$ lies in `ssJSet q κ`; the hypothesis `hle` records the inclusion of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` (the subfield of Laurent series over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ generated by the coefficientwise images of `modularFunctionFieldFull M'`) in `fieldBar q M'` (the corresponding base change of the $X_H$ function field at level $q^2M'$ for $H$ the kernel of $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times$). The datum $R_0$ is a `ConstantReduction` of $A$ from `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` to `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'` — a valuation subring $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$, a surjective residue homomorphism onto `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'` with kernel the maximal ideal, a map on places preserving degrees, and the compatibilities with $A$ and with orders of functions recorded in that structure — and `hR₀` demands that for every Laurent series $y$ over $A$ whose coefficientwise image in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ lies in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, that image lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ and its $R_0$-residue is, as a Laurent series over $\kappa$, the coefficientwise reduction of $y$. Finally $s$ is a chosen element of $W$, i.e. a supersingular place.
--
--   The block of small constants consists of: an intermediate field $k_0$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q}$ and an element $\pi_0 \in k_0$ lying in $A$, such that $A_0 := A \cap k_0$ (the comap of $A$ along $k_0 \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$) is a discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$, is Henselian, and has algebraically closed residue field; together with `hκ`, which asks that every $a \in A$ be congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to some element of $k_0 \cap A$. To this is added an auxiliary prime $\ell$ with $\ell \geq 3$, $\ell \neq q$ and $\ell \nmid M'$, an element $\zeta_0 \in k_0$ which is a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, and an element $\varpi_t \in k_0 \cap A$ with $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1} = q\,u$ for some unit $u$ of $A$. The base layer consists of an intermediate field $K_b$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/k_0$ required to be the bottom one (so $K_b = k_0$), a valuation subring $A_b$ of $K_b$ whose members are exactly the elements lying in $A$, and a non-zero generator $\varpi_b$ of the maximal ideal of $A_b$.
--
--   The conclusion is stated for the algebra structure of $k_0$ on `fieldBar q M'` obtained by composing $k_0 \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} \to$ `fieldBar q M'`. It asserts: for every intermediate field $F_0$ of `fieldBar q M'` over $k_0$ satisfying the four level-field clauses
--   (F1) $f \in F_0$ if and only if every Laurent coefficient of $f$ lies in (the image of) $k_0$;
--   (F2) the join of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ is all of `fieldBar q M'`;
--   (F3) for every $\zeta \in$ `Idx q` (a primitive $q$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$) and every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$, the automorphism `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` maps $F_0$ into itself;
--   (F4) linear disjointness: for every finite extension $K'$ of $k_0$ inside $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, every $m$, every $c : \mathrm{Fin}\,m \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ linearly independent over $K'$ and every $a : \mathrm{Fin}\,m \to$ `fieldBar q M'` with all $a_i$ in the join of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $K'$, the relation $\sum_i c_i a_i = 0$ forces $a_i = 0$ for all $i$;
--   and for every valuation subring $W_0$ of $F_0$ satisfying the following six clauses:
--   (W1) for $x \in k_0$, $x \in A$ if and only if the image of $x$ in $F_0$ lies in $W_0$;
--   (W2) $W_0$ is a discrete valuation ring;
--   (W3) the image of $\pi_0$ lies in $W_0$ and generates its maximal ideal;
--   (W4) the clause placing $W_0$ over $s$: for every Laurent series $g$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ in `modularFunctionFieldFull M'` whose coefficientwise image $\bar g$ in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$, if at every place $P$ of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ the inequality $0 \le P.\mathrm{ord}(\overline{\mathtt{jq}})$ implies $0 \le P.\mathrm{ord}(\bar g)$, and if the $R_0$-residue of $\bar g$ lies in the valuation subring of the place $s$, then the image of $\bar g$ in `fieldBar q M'` lies in $F_0$, the resulting element lies in $W_0$, and for every $c \in k_0 \cap A$ whose residue in $\kappa$ equals $s.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of the $R_0$-residue of $\bar g$, the difference of that element and the image of $c$ lies in $W_0$ and in the maximal ideal of $W_0$;
--   (W5) for every $\zeta$, every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ and every $f \in F_0$ with `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` $f \in F_0$: $f \in W_0$ if and only if its image lies in $W_0$;
--   (W6) the model clause: there exist a subring $B$ of `fieldBar q M'` and an $A_b$-algebra structure on $B$ such that the structure map sends $a \in A_b$ to the image of $a$ under $K_b \subseteq \overline{\mathbb{Q}} \to$ `fieldBar q M'`; $B$ is contained in the join $L$ of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $K_b$, and every element of $L$ is of the form $g/h$ with $g, h \in B$, $h \neq 0$; $B$ is formally smooth and of finite presentation over $A_b$; $B/\varpi_b B$ has Krull dimension at most $1$; every element of $B$ lies in $F_0$ and in $W_0$; the image of $\varpi_b$ is prime in $B$; an element of $F_0$ lies in $W_0$ precisely when it is $g/h$ with $g,h \in B$ and the image of $\varpi_b$ not dividing $h$; the image of `jq` lies in $B$; $B$ is stable under `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` for all $\zeta$ and all $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$; and, for every algebra structure of `GaloisField q 2` on $\kappa$, every witness that [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q κ`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) is a domain, and every $\zeta \in$ `Idx q`, there are a subgroup $C_s$ of the $(q+1)$-st roots of unity of `GaloisField q 2` and a ring homomorphism $\rho$ from $B$ to [`DrinfeldCurve.quotField q κ Cs`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelSemistableCoveringW2.html#L32) (the fixed field, inside the fraction field of `CoordRing q κ`, of the subgroup generated by the actions of the elements $(1,\zeta')$, $\zeta' \in C_s$) with: $\mathrm{card}\,C_s =$ `placeWidthChar q M'` of $s$ (which, as $q = 2$, is $12$ or $1$ according as the value of the geometric $j$-generator at $s$ vanishes or not, divided by the ramification index `placeRamificationJ M'` of $j$ at $s$); $\ker \rho$ the ideal generated by the image of $\varpi_b$; $\rho$ compatible with reduction $A_b \to \kappa$ on the image of $A_b$; every element of the target a ratio $\rho g/\rho h$ with $\rho h \neq 0$; the image of $\rho$ consisting exactly of those elements of the target which, viewed in the Drinfeld function field, lie in the image of `CoordRing q κ`; and the equivariance $\rho(\mathtt{levelAutBar q M' ζ}\,\gamma^{-1} f) =$ [`DrinfeldCurve.hFunctionFieldAction q κ`](def/DrinfeldCurve_FunctionField.html#L16) at $(\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma, 1)$ applied to $\rho f$, for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ with $(\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma, 1) \in$ [`DrinfeldCurve.hSubgroup q`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L276) and $f \in B$ with `levelAutBar q M' ζ` $\gamma^{-1} f \in B$;
--   the following nine statements hold.
--
--   First, the join of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ is all of `fieldBar q M'`, exactly clause (F2). Second, for $x \in k_0$, $x \in A$ if and only if its image lies in $W_0$, exactly (W1). Third, $W_0$ is a discrete valuation ring, exactly (W2). Fourth, the image of $\pi_0$ lies in $W_0$ and generates its maximal ideal, exactly (W3). Fifth — the one assertion not among the hypotheses — there exists $t \in W_0$ such that for every polynomial $p$ over $k_0$ all of whose coefficients lie in $A$, if $p(t)$ lies in $W_0$ and in the maximal ideal of $W_0$ then every coefficient of $p$ has image lying in $W_0$ and in its maximal ideal; that is, the residue of $t$ is transcendental over the residue field of $A_0$. Sixth, the clause (W4) placing $W_0$ over the supersingular place $s$, verbatim. Seventh, for every $\zeta \in$ `Idx q` and every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$, both the stability of $F_0$ under `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` as in (F3) and the equivalence of (W5). Eighth, the linear-disjointness clause (F4), verbatim. Ninth, the model clause (W6), verbatim, with the same eleven items including the identification of the special fibre through the Drinfeld curve and its level equivariance.
--
--   This is the functorial read-off step of the construction of the semistable model of the modular curve of level $q^2M'$ at a supersingular point in the case $q = 2$ with a rigidifying prime $\ell_g \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ dividing $M'$: given a level field $F_0$ over the small constants $k_0$, a valuation ring $W_0$ over the supersingular place $s$ and an affine chart $B$ over $A \cap k_0$ whose special fibre is cut out of the Drinfeld curve, it returns the complete package, the residual-transcendence clause being supplied by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.supersingularDVR_residuallyTranscendental_of_affineChart_of_eq_two_of_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.supersingularDVR_residuallyTranscendental_of_affineChart_of_eq_two_of_dvd). It feeds the existence statement [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_klevel_supersingularDVR_smoothPointPackages_nodePresentations_nodeCharts_hasseJ_drinfeldInertia_of_eq_two_of_dvd_affineChart`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_klevel_supersingularDVR_smoothPointPackages_nodePresentations_nodeCharts_hasseJ_drinfeldInertia_of_eq_two_of_dvd_affineChart).
